ect aims to create a fully functional Catan game with both single-player (vs AI opponents) and multiplayer capabilities.\n\n### Architecture\n\n**Monorepo structure using npm workspaces:**\n\n| Package | Purpose | Tech Stack |\n|---------|---------|------------|\n| `game/` | Core game engine (pure TypeScript) | TypeScript, no framework dependencies |\n| `ui/` | React frontend | React 18, Vite, TypeScript |\n| `server/` | Backend WebSocket server | Node.js, Express, TypeScript (to be implemented) |\n| `shared/` | Shared utilities | TypeScript |\n\n**Key Design Principle:** The core game logic (`catan-game`) is a pure TypeScript module with no framework dependencies. Both frontend and backend import this module, ensuring:\n- Consistent rules across all environments\n- Single-player offline play without backend\n- Single source of truth for game logic\n\n## Current Implementation Status\n\n### ✅ Completed Components\n\n1. **Core Game Engine (`game/`)**\n   - Board generation with hexagonal grid (19 hexes, radius 2)\n   - Terrain distribution (4 forest, 3 hills, 4 pastures, 4 fields, 3 mountains, 1 desert)\n   - Number tokens (2-12, excluding 7) with adjacency constraints\n   - Complete `Game` class with:\n     - Setup phase (initial settlements/roads placement)\n     - Play phase (dice rolling, resource distribution)\n     - All core game actions (build road/settlement/city, move robber, development cards)\n   - AI opponent system (`ComputerOpponent` class) with heuristic-based decision making\n   - Victory point tracking (10 VP win condition)\n\n2. **Enhanced Data Structures** ⭐ NEW\n   - `types.ts`: Comprehensive interfaces for modern data model\n     - `Harbor[]` array instead of vertex properties\n     - ResourceObject plain objects instead of Maps\n     - Development cards split into `hand[]` and `played[]` arrays\n     - Hidden victory points tracking\n     - TradeOffer and CompletedTrade interfaces\n   \n   - `stateManager.ts`: Utility functions for state manipulation\n     - `calculateVictoryPoints()` - authoritative VP calculation\n     - `calculateLeaderboard()` - sorted player rankings\n     - Resource helpers (hasResources, deductResources, addResources)\n     - Harbor utilities (getPlayerHarbors, canUseHarbor, getHarborAtVertex)\n     - Development card deck management\n     - Longest road calculation using BFS\n\n3. **Frontend (`ui/`)**\n   - React 18 + Vite setup\n   - `GameContext` for state management\n   - Board rendering with hexagonal tiles (HTML5/CSS)\n   - Player info panel (resources, VP, cards)\n   - Action panel for player interactions\n\n4. **Server Skeleton (`server/`)**\n   - Project structure created with directories for:\n     - `ws/` - WebSocket handling\n     - `game/` - Game room management\n     - `types/` - Server-side types\n   - *Note: Implementation pending*\n\n### 🚧 Pending Tasks\n\n1. **Backend Implementation**\n   - Express server with WebSocket endpoint\n   - Game room management and session handling\n   - Action validation and state broadcasting\n   - Player authentication (JWT)\n   - Database integration (PostgreSQL for persistence, Redis for sessions)\n\n2. **Frontend Enhancements**\n   - WebSocket client integration for multiplayer\n   - Complete action panel UI (build, trade, development cards)\n   - Reconnection handling and state sync\n\n3. **AI Improvements**\n   - Refine heuristic algorithms\n   - Add difficulty levels\n   - Implement trading AI\n\n4. **Testing**\n   - Unit tests for game logic (Vitest)\n   - Integration tests for WebSocket protocol\n   - UI component tests (React Testing Library)\n\n## Building and Running\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Node.js (v18+)\n- npm (v8+)\n\n### Commands\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies (from project root)\nnpm install\n\n# Build both game engine and UI\nnpm run build\n\n# Start the development UI (single-player mode)\nnpm run start\n\n# Run tests (when implemented)\nnpm test\n```\n\n### Development Workflow\n\n1. **Single-Player Mode:**\n   ```bash\n   npm run start\n   ```\n   Runs Vite dev server with local game engine. AI opponents handle their turns automatically.\n\n2. **Multiplayer Mode (when backend is complete):**\n   - Start backend server\n   - Frontend connects via WebSocket\n   - Multiple clients can join game rooms\n\n## Game Rules Summary\n\n### Board Setup\n- 19 hexagonal tiles in a radius-2 hexagonal grid\n- Terrain: 4 forest (wood), 3 hills (brick), 4 pastures (sheep), 4 fields (wheat), 3 mountains (ore), 1 desert\n- Number tokens placed on 18 non-desert hexes (no two identical tokens adjacent)\n- Robber starts on desert\n\n### Game Phases\n1. **Setup Phase:** Players alternate placing initial settlements and roads\n2. **Play Phase:** Main game loop with dice rolling, resource collection, building, trading\n3. **End Phase:** Game ends when a player reaches 10 victory points\n\n### Victory Conditions\n- Settlement: 1 VP\n- City: 2 VP\n- Longest Road: 2 VP\n- Largest Army: 2 VP\n- Victory Point Cards: 1 VP each\n- **Win condition: 10 VP**\n\n### Core Actions\n- `rollDice()` - Roll dice, collect resources based on production\n- `buildRoad(edgeId)` - Build road on unowned edge (wood + brick)\n- `buildSettlement(vertexId)` - Build settlement on unoccupied vertex (wood + brick + wheat + sheep)\n- `buildCity(vertexId)` - Upgrade settlement to city (2 wheat + 3 ore)\n- `moveRobber(hexId)` - Move robber, steal from adjacent players\n- `buyDevelopmentCard()` - Purchase random development card\n- `playDevelopmentCard(type)` - Play knight, monopoly, year of plenty, etc.\n- `endTurn()` - End turn, pass dice to next player\n\n## AI Opponent System\n\nThe `ComputerOpponent` class implements heuristic-based decision making:\n\n1. **Setup Phase:** Prioritizes vertices with high-probability number tokens and resource diversity\n2. **Play Phase:**\n   - Builds cities first (higher VP yield)\n   - Expands road network for connectivity\n   - Uses development cards strategically\n   - Moves robber to disrupt leading players\n\n**Single-Player Mode:** AI opponents automatically take their turns, allowing you to play against them.\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\n/home/atmandk/play/\n├── game/                    # Core game engine\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── types.ts         # Type definitions (enhanced)\n│   │   ├── board.ts         # Board generation with harbors array\n│   │   ├── gameState.ts     # Game class implementation\n│   │   ├── ai.ts            # AI opponent logic\n│   │   └── stateManager.ts  # State management utilities ⭐ NEW\n│   └── package.json\n├── ui/                      # React frontend\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── App.tsx          # Main app component\n│   │   ├── Board.tsx        # Board rendering with harbor support\n│   │   ├── HexTile.tsx      # Individual hex component\n│   │   └── contexts/\n│   │       └── GameContext.tsx  # State management (updated)\n│   └── package.json\n├── server/                   # Backend (skeleton)\n│   └── src/\n│       ├── ws/              # WebSocket handlers\n│       ├── game/            # Game room logic\n│       └── types/           # Server types\n├── shared/                   # Shared utilities\n├── DESIGN.md                 # Detailed design document\n├── package.json              # Workspace root\n└── LOWCAL.md                 # This file\n```\n\n## Development Conventions\n\n### Code Style\n- TypeScript strict mode enabled\n- ES modules (import/export)\n- Functional programming patterns where appropriate\n- Comprehensive error handling\n\n### Testing Strategy (planned)\n- Unit tests for game logic using Vitest\n- Integration tests for WebSocket protocol\n- UI component tests with React Testing Library\n\n### Git Workflow\n- Feature branches for new functionality\n- Pull requests for code review\n- Commit messages follow conventional commits\n\n## Data Structure Reference\n\n### Harbor Interface ⭐ NEW\n```typescript\ninterface Harbor {\n  vertexId: number;           // Primary vertex ID (harbor shared between two vertices)\n  type: HarborType;           // 'resource' or 'generic'\n  resource?: Resource;        // For resource harbors (wood, brick, sheep, wheat, ore)\n  ratio: 2 | 3;               // 2 for resource harbors, 3 for generic\n}\n```\n\n### Resource Object ⭐ NEW\n```typescript\ntype ResourceObject = {\n  wood: number;\n  brick: number;\n  sheep: number;\n  wheat: number;\n  ore: number;\n};\n```\n\n### Development Cards Structure ⭐ UPDATED\n```typescript\ninterface Player {\n  developmentCards: {\n    hand: DevelopmentCardInHand[];     // Unplayed cards in player's possession\n    played: DevelopmentCardPlayed[];   // Cards that have been played\n  };\n}\n```\n\n## Git History\n\n| Commit | Date | Description |\n| fb95cc7 | Mar 13, 2026 | feat: Complete robber implementation with hex click handler and SVG rendering - Add handleHexClick() function in App.tsx that calls game.moveRobber(), pass onHexClick and mustMoveRobber props to Board component, render custom robber SVG graphic on hexes when hasRobber is true, make hexes clickable when mustMoveRobber flag is set. The robber can now be moved by clicking on hex tiles after rolling a 7 or playing a knight card.\n| 1dc3916 | Mar 13, 2026 | feat: Complete harbor data structure refactoring and UI updates - Major architectural improvements including Harbor[] array instead of vertex properties, ResourceObject plain objects instead of Maps, state property name updates (turnIndex→turnNumber), and comprehensive stateManager.ts utilities. All builds pass. |\n| 6545e95 | Mar 12, 2026 | fix(ui): Resolve setup phase completion bug - Fixed critical issue in GameContext where lastProcessedRef was updated with stale state values after AI turns. Now correctly updates ref with NEW game state after each AI turn completes. Setup phase now successfully progresses to play phase in all player configurations (2, 3, 4 players). |\n| 5c097d0 | Mar 11, 2026 | docs: Update LOWCAL.md with new UI enhancements and project status |\n| b90533b | Mar 11, 2026 | feat(ui): Enhance game UI with modern aesthetics and quickstart mode - Add ?quickstart=true parameter to bypass configuration screen, implement DiceDisplay component for graphical dice rendering, enhanced board visuals with gradient terrain tiles drop shadows and glowing tokens, modern player list sidebar with animated turn indicator, updated fonts (Nunito, Quicksand) and gradient styling |\n| f36659c | Mar 10, 2026 | Fix setup phase AI turn processing for 3+ players - Fixed AI opponent to correctly process dice rolls when multiple players are involved in the same game session |\n| dd695c0 | Mar 10, 2026 | fix: move harbor rendering before settlements to fix dock line visibility - Ensured harbor circles render before settlement/city nodes so connection lines appear behind them |\n| 8214ed2 | Mar 10, 2026 | fix: harbor placement algorithm for proper spacing and randomization - Improved harbor placement to ensure proper spacing between harbors and correct randomization of resource types |\n| e5f2e3a | Mar 9, 2026 | Fix harbor placement and settlement adjacency validation - Fixed issues with harbor placement conflicting with settlement adjacency rules |\n| f5fdb35 | Mar 4, 2026 | Add allowedHosts configuration for Tailscale access |\n| aae2efd | Mar 4, 2026 | Fix harbor placement to prevent adjacent harbors from sharing nodes |\n| 8b97110 | Mar 3, 2026 | Configure server for Tailnet access (WebSocket server, static UI serving) |\n| need07b | Mar 3, 2026 | Fix resource harbor ratios to 2:1 per Catan rules |\n| ac115af | Feb 26, 2026 | Initial commit: Settlers of Catan implementation |\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **Backend incomplete:** Multiplayer functionality requires server implementation\n2. **UI polish:** Some animations and visual feedback still needed\n3. **AI depth:** Heuristic AI can be improved with machine learning\n4. **No database:** Game state not persisted between sessions\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n- [ ] Complete backend with WebSocket multiplayer\n- [ ] Add chat functionality\n- [ ] Implement trading UI\n- [ ] Add sound effects and animations\n- [ ] Create mobile-responsive design\n- [ ] Add game history and replay feature\n- [ ] Implement ranked matchmaking\n- [ ] Add unit tests for all game logic\n- [ ] Implement full longest road calculation (BFS)\n\n---\n\n*Last updated: March 13, 2026*\n*Project Status: Core engine complete with enhanced data structures. UI fully functional with modern aesthetics and **robber movement system**. Harbors now stored in separate Harbor[] array instead of vertex properties. Resources use plain ResourceObject instead of Maps. Victory points calculated dynamically via calculateVictoryPoints(). All builds pass successfully.*\n--- End of Context from: LOWCAL.md ---"
